From a22b13eb75743cf48bd0fdedfbc57cfe4a61217e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:54:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/65] Switch Vulkan: decode new sprites in the background,
 save warm list at once

- vk_asynctex: sprite pictures that are not on the GPU yet are decoded on
  the nx_jobs worker (core 2); the game thread copies finished ones to the
  GPU within a budget and leaves the sprite out until then. Actor classes
  are prefetched when they first appear (rd_vk_async_textures).
- hw_nxprefetch: the border trim of a new sprite (a full decode on the game
  or render thread) runs on the worker too (rd_async_sprites); class
  prefetches go through a queue pumped 0.75 ms per frame.
- nx_jobs: URGENT priority for sounds, which LoadSound may block on.
- texture warm list saved one second after a new entry; the background
  writer writes queued files within 0.25 s (short sessions lost the list).
- perf.log: player think, spawns, StartSound, skipped sprites, and a note
  for every state action that takes 5 ms or more (with script file:line);
  session report counts upload overflow waits and blit upload failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
